[seller.step] write · agent (claude-haiku-5-5): Packaged LibreOffice headless as a stdlib-only converter. convert.py validates the input (extension, readability, 25 MiB limit, zip/XML or RTF header integrity), copies it into a private temp dir with the document title set to its metadata title or the file stem, and converts it with LibreOffice using PDF/A-2b (SelectPdfVersion=2). Each run uses its own LibreOffice profile so concurrent runs work. Exit codes: 0 success, 2 unsupported or unreadable/corrupt input, 3 over 25 MiB, 4 timeout (60 s, overridable via CONVERT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS for tests). Spreadsheets export all sheets through the Calc PDF filter. tests/make_fixtures.py builds minimal docx/odt/rtf/pptx/xlsx files with the standard library, and tests/test_convert.py covers conversion, PDF/A marker, text, title rules, non-ASCII names, exit codes and concurrency, writing only to pytest tmp_path. Caveats: I have not executed this in the sandbox, so the pytest run and the minimal pptx/xlsx fixtures are unverified. ODT or OOXML files without a metadata part get the stem as title rather than a metadata title, because the converter does not add missing metadata parts.
